  "summary": "Your messages queue is clear: all 7 refill messages are closed. One of them, a second pharmacy request for Samuel Price's metformin, came in while I was working. Three results also arrived during the work and changed decisions for all three patients. I corrected those decisions under RBC-RX-05 §7.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). The patient's message and both pharmacy requests were handled as one request. Corrected eGFR is 58; HbA1c was 7.1% at an outside lab on 2026-08-19.\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled.** I renewed it first (mr-t0001), then cancelled it when the creatinine from the 2026-10-06 BMP was corrected to 1.49. That is 35% above the 1.10 before the dose was raised on 9/18, and the policy treats it like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n- Urgent review task for you: task-t0013, focused on mr-00295.\n- Patient sent a correction message.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027)**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled.** The August potassium of 5.9 was from a hemolyzed sample and didn't count, so I renewed it first (mr-t0003) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0006). Then a St. Brigid BMP from 10/20 arrived with a good sample and potassium 5.8, so I cancelled the refill.\n- Urgent review task for you: task-t0014, focused on mr-00283. His hernia repair is now scheduled for 11/12.\n- Patient sent a correction message.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0005). The eGFR of 39 from 10/14 was entered in error and not used.\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg:** his last BMP was over 12 months old, so I first gave a 30-day supply (mr-t0004) and ordered a BMP (sr-t0007). A valid BMP from 10/22 then arrived (potassium 4.6), so I replaced it with a 90-day supply with 1 refill (mr-t0015).\n- Patient sent an update message.\n\nI wrote a phone note for each patient, citing RBC-RX-05.\n\n**Still needs your attention**\n- Because each refill replaced the existing order, the original lisinopril orders for Mr. Price and Mr. Odum (mr-00295, mr-00283) now show as stopped. Neither patient has an active lisinopril order until you decide.\n- Mr. Webb's BMP order (sr-t0007) is no longer needed, but I couldn't cancel it with the tools I have. Please discontinue it.\n- Mr. Odum's repeat BMP order (sr-t0006) is still active, which may be useful given his potassium.\n- In your results queue, the three new items behind these changes (inbox-a0001, a0003, a0004) are still open: I acted on them but didn't close them, since only the messages queue was in scope. The 8 older results items there, including two critical potassiums (pt-0016 at 6.3, pt-0008 at 6.4), were outside this request and haven't been touched.",
